# vehje-signature. backlog

Designed but deferred. Names stay unbackticked until they ship.

## The full lens-projection differential check

The handoff from the Rust-emitted data to the specialised Zig runtime ships in
its cheaper content-addressed manifest-check interim (the manifest binds the
package to the runtime and a differential harness checks the projection). The
full one-source-two-projections lens (both sides generated projections of the
signature, differential-checked structurally rather than by manifest hash) is
the open handoff-staging question and lands here when it lands.

## The introduction-compiled stencil projection

The third projection (operations compiled to copy-and-patch machine-code
stencils) has its schema slot in the signature from day one, but its producer
is the deferred stencil toolchain. The signature names the slot; the bytes come
later.

## Fold into runtime-gen if the consumer set collapses

If the only real consumer of the signature contract turns out to be the
packaging crate (that is, if the check pass ends up taking lease rules as
runtime values fed by the orchestrator rather than reading the signature), this
crate shrinks to a data shim and folds into vehje-runtime-gen. It is kept a
crate because the check pass reads its lease-rule schema and axiom table and
because ecosystem grammar-as-data tooling and the proof document both want a
citable one-source language-definition contract.
